3. The brief facts of the present case are that on 16.12.2004, the Food Inspector Sh.Sanjeev Kumar Gupta and Sh. Brahma Nand, Field Assistant under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh. Harish Kumar Ahuja, reached at the premises of appellant i.e. M/s Royal Caterers at Khasra No.
1012, Prem Nagar II, Kirari, Delhi, where the accused/vendor was found conducting business of food articles and having stored Sela Rice ; which was lying in an open small gunny bag without label or declaration meant for preparation of cooked rice to be served to MCD School children. ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to take sample of commodity from the vendor which was lying in an open small gunny bag bearing no label declaration, to which he agreed ;
- that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor/appellant and offer towards the sale price of sample, to which he agreed, however, not accepted the sale consideration, sample was then lifted for analysis;
CA no. 8729/16 Ajay Kr. Gupta @ Ajay Kumar Vs. Food Inspector (PFA) pages 2 of 13 - that each sample was separately packed, fastened, marked, sealed and necessary documents including Notice as per Form-VI in the presence of appellant/accused alongwith Panchnama etc was prepared at the spot ; the price of the sample commodity was not paid to the vendor ;
- that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 30.12.2004, PA found the sample to be adulterated on the ground that it was coloured with synthetic colouring matter "Sunset Yellow FCF" and 'Tartrazine';
- that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by Food Inspector and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.

The complaint was then filed in the court on 07.03.2005 alleging violation of Section 2(ia),(j) and (m) of PFA Act r/w Rules 23, 28 & 29 of PFA Rules, as punishable under Section 7/16(1A) of PFA. Act.
- that the complaint was filed in writing by a public servant, hence, recording of pre-summoning evidence was dispensed with ;
